From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:24:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: dependency licence scan and check actions

licence-scan runs a pinned, checksum-verified osv-scanner on committed
lockfiles (pnpm, uv, NuGet and the rest it reads) and freezes packages,
licences, lockfiles and manifests without a lockfile into a fingerprinted
packet. licence-check judges that packet with no network: SPDX
expressions against an allow/review/deny policy, with exact-version
overrides that must cite evidence. Codes stay advisory; the consuming
workflow decides to fail.

The scanner pin is empty until a release and its SHA-256 are recorded;
until then the scan reports itself incomplete.

